Z||000000||80's BOY||05-13-2001||10:21 PM||||after doing some donuts in the GT i was driving home and noticed this....the car now stays in 1st gear until it redlines then BUMPS into 3rd hard. i also have no passing gears. when i floor it what should be a downshift acts like neutral and when i let off it BUMPS back in gear. at 30mph tests i can feel 2nd try to push but it's like it tries and then redlines again. maybe a burnt intermediate gear is the problem? keep in mind that my fluids are fine, but i'm not sure about the TV cable. maybe i pulled the cable or something. the fluid WAS low when i was playing around so in retrospect i should've checked it earlier. please give some info if anyone has any. i'm really worried this time. also how hard is it to change out the gears with the tranny in the car?? hope someone has some info. thanks again.<P>||||reg||13
Z||000001||robertjay||05-13-2001||11:37 PM||||Check for any stored codes, on newer GM trannys, the ECM will store codes, but not turn on your check engine light.  I am repairing the transmission in my truck for a similar problem.  I had a very slushy /non existent 3rd gear, and not much reverse.  It happened when I put her in reverse before I was totally stopped (turned the wrong way down a one way).  I ended up blowing the application piston for the direct drive clutch pack.  It's aluminum, and apparently breaks a lot on Chevys.<P>I have a factory service manual, but I can't find it right now after the move.  I'm not sure how "electronic" Fiero Auto trannys are, but usually if you have one gear that doesn't work, and the others bang real hard, it's because the computer sensed an incorrect ratio between the input sensor and output sensor in any given gear.  If that happens, it automatically jacks the pressure full bore, so it makes the good gears hit real hard.<P>Not trying to scare you, it's just that I can really relate right now after going through the same thing.  Anyway, I would try to check for any codes, do a search on transmission trouble codes for GM and you should be able to find a good explanation of each one, if there are any stored.<P>Good Luck!<P>PS, my truck is a '95 1-ton Dually Chevy, I'm pretty sure the basic operation of GM electornic trannies are very similar.<p>[This message has been edited by robertjay (edited 05-13-2001).]||||reg||1
